00:25:13,162 --> 00:25:17,249
HAN is the most sought-after brand
in the Paris fashion scene.

266
00:25:17,333 --> 00:25:21,379
Hold on. Is HAN the brand
SE is trying to partner with?

267
00:25:21,462 --> 00:25:23,881
This is insane.

268
00:25:24,173 --> 00:25:26,968
The only way
to turn this crisis around is

269
00:25:28,636 --> 00:25:30,137
if we snatch HAN first.

270
00:25:35,434 --> 00:25:37,103
We'll be setting up
a special task force.

271
00:25:37,895 --> 00:25:40,022
Anyone's welcome to join.

272
00:25:41,691 --> 00:25:43,985
That's going to be tough.

273
00:25:56,914 --> 00:25:58,708
POP-UP EVENT PERFORMANCE REPORT

274
00:26:43,461 --> 00:26:46,839
<i>I've forwarded the access logs
and CCTV screenshots to your email.</i>

275
00:26:56,766 --> 00:26:58,434
Holy cow.

276
00:26:58,809 --> 00:27:00,603
This is a massive scoop.

277
00:27:00,686 --> 00:27:03,272
- I heard from the security room...
- Shush.

278
00:27:03,355 --> 00:27:04,440
- Come.
- What?

279
00:27:09,403 --> 00:27:11,572
- Is that Hye-soo?
- Yes.

280
00:27:12,364 --> 00:27:13,365
Is she the one?

281
00:27:17,411 --> 00:27:18,412
Ms. Seo.

282
00:27:19,121 --> 00:27:21,624
You know that personal email usage
is prohibited at work, right?

283
00:27:22,750 --> 00:27:25,544
- Yes, sir.
- Why'd you break security protocol?

284
00:27:28,089 --> 00:27:29,590
I can't quite remember...

285
00:27:31,175 --> 00:27:33,636
Why are you asking me this?

286
00:27:42,478 --> 00:27:44,396
Oh, that's...

287
00:27:47,900 --> 00:27:51,654
Don't tell me
you're accusing me of being the spy.

288
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:55,699
I swear it's not me.

289
00:27:55,783 --> 00:27:57,952
Me, a spy?
That's absolutely ridiculous!

290
00:27:58,035 --> 00:28:00,704
Spy or not, the dating scandal photos

291
00:28:01,372 --> 00:28:02,623
certainly look like your doing.

292
00:28:19,515 --> 00:28:20,724
This is for you.

293
00:28:25,354 --> 00:28:26,355
I'm sorry.

294
00:28:28,232 --> 00:28:29,275
What...

295
00:28:31,068 --> 00:28:33,863
Mr. Kang, could you
check this for me?

296
00:28:34,864 --> 00:28:38,075
<i>You flat-out rejected
my feelings for you.</i>

297
00:28:43,122 --> 00:28:44,623
- What?
- I don't need it.

298
00:28:44,707 --> 00:28:45,958
Then, buy me one.

299
00:28:49,336 --> 00:28:51,297
<i>Then I saw you
meeting privately with Da-reum.</i>

300
00:28:52,381 --> 00:28:53,382
<i>It made me so mad.</i>

301
00:28:56,844 --> 00:28:59,680
Some reporter handed me
a business card.

302
00:29:02,099 --> 00:29:05,269
- I had no idea it'd get this big.
- Ms. Seo.

303
00:29:05,978 --> 00:29:08,689
Are you aware of how much
this has cost the company?

304
00:29:10,482 --> 00:29:11,525
I'm so sorry.

305
00:29:11,609 --> 00:29:13,277
CEO KANG HA-GI

306
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:14,987
You'll be disciplined
according to company policy.

307
00:29:15,654 --> 00:29:16,739
And...

308
00:29:18,991 --> 00:29:21,243
I suggest
you reflect on who truly deserves

309
00:29:22,745 --> 00:29:23,996
your apology.

310
00:30:02,034 --> 00:30:03,994
- Goodness.
- Good grief.

311
00:30:34,525 --> 00:30:37,820
- Oh, my. Thank you.
- I'm more grateful.

312
00:30:42,574 --> 00:30:44,451
I caught her thanks to your tip-off.

313
00:30:46,203 --> 00:30:49,623
I'm basically
a walking security camera, you know.

314
00:30:51,417 --> 00:30:54,586
Ms. Seo isn't the spy, though.
She just leaked the photos.

315
00:30:54,670 --> 00:30:55,838
Oh, really?

316
00:30:56,380 --> 00:30:58,841
Then, who is the real spy?

317
00:31:01,260 --> 00:31:03,929
Regardless, thank you for your help.

318
00:31:10,728 --> 00:31:13,647
Mr. Kang, I'll keep an eye out.

319
00:31:26,827 --> 00:31:27,995
Why, that little...

320
00:31:28,454 --> 00:31:30,956
I'm here to deliver fried chicken,
not take out the trash.

321
00:31:31,790 --> 00:31:35,627
Seriously, where on earth is Roy?

322
00:31:38,505 --> 00:31:39,798
QUICK DELIVERY
DRIVE SAFELY

323
00:31:40,466 --> 00:31:43,844
Jeez. Watch where you're going!

324
00:31:43,927 --> 00:31:44,970
Are you okay?

325
00:31:45,888 --> 00:31:48,015
<i>Wait, this voice...</i>

326
00:31:49,308 --> 00:31:50,476
Are you hurt?

327
00:31:51,060 --> 00:31:52,186
<i>Roy?</i>

328
00:31:55,939 --> 00:31:58,650
Oh, this is killing me. My back...

329
00:31:58,734 --> 00:32:00,861
Goodness, my hip.

330
00:32:01,403 --> 00:32:03,405
You're not even showing your face.

331
00:32:03,489 --> 00:32:05,032
Are you trying to pull a hit-and-run?

332
00:32:05,115 --> 00:32:07,993
A hit-and-run?
No, it's nothing like that.

333
00:32:08,744 --> 00:32:13,040
Then take off that helmet
and apologize properly.

334
00:32:19,463 --> 00:32:21,173
<i>Take it off.</i>

335
00:32:21,548 --> 00:32:23,092
<i>Come on. Please take it off.</i>

336
00:32:42,569 --> 00:32:44,822
I'm sorry. I was careless.

337
00:32:45,614 --> 00:32:46,698
I apologize.

338
00:32:47,491 --> 00:32:48,617
Here.

339
00:33:00,546 --> 00:33:02,381
What? Oh, thanks.

340
00:33:09,221 --> 00:33:11,557
Are you badly hurt?
Shall we go to the ER?

341
00:33:11,640 --> 00:33:14,309
No, I'm fine.

342
00:33:14,393 --> 00:33:15,519
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

343
00:33:18,730 --> 00:33:20,107
- You can let go now.
- Right.

344
00:33:26,530 --> 00:33:28,991
The brand HAN is really fascinating.

345
00:33:29,533 --> 00:33:32,077
The Creative Director's identity is
under wraps.

346
00:33:32,161 --> 00:33:34,788
All they have on social media is
their brand account.

347
00:33:34,872 --> 00:33:37,332
I think that's what piques
everyone's curiosity.

348
00:33:39,126 --> 00:33:41,753
That's enough for now.
Let's go eat. I'm starving.

349
00:33:41,837 --> 00:33:43,964
- Good idea.
- Yes, let's eat.

350
00:33:44,047 --> 00:33:45,716
Do you see this, everyone?

351
00:33:45,799 --> 00:33:46,884
What does it look like?

352
00:33:47,426 --> 00:33:50,512
I have the corporate credit card
in my hands.

353
00:33:51,054 --> 00:33:53,682
- What do you want to eat?
<i>- Budae-jjigae.</i>

354
00:33:53,765 --> 00:33:56,143
<i>- Budae-jjigae? </i>Let's go eat, then.
- Great.

355
00:33:56,226 --> 00:33:58,103
Let's go. Let's go downstairs.

356
00:33:58,187 --> 00:33:59,354
<i>- Budae-jjigae.</i>
- What else?

357
00:33:59,438 --> 00:34:01,982
Spicy stir-fried webfoot octopus.

358
00:34:02,065 --> 00:34:04,485
- Come on. Let's go.
- Gosh...

359
00:34:09,323 --> 00:34:11,992
- Da-reum, you coming?
- Yes. I am.

360
00:34:34,765 --> 00:34:35,891
She's an outcast.

361
00:34:36,433 --> 00:34:38,644
She brought it on herself.

362
00:34:49,863 --> 00:34:50,948
Ms. Seo.

363
00:34:51,573 --> 00:34:53,617
Can I have a word?

364
00:34:56,954 --> 00:34:58,080
Okay.

365
00:35:03,210 --> 00:35:05,504
What was that?
Are they having a fight?

366
00:35:18,559 --> 00:35:19,560
Ms. Seo.

367
00:35:20,727 --> 00:35:21,853
What do you want?

368
00:35:25,941 --> 00:35:28,735
What are you doing?
Are you going to beat me up?

369
00:35:31,572 --> 00:35:35,117
No, wait, sorry. I'm really sorry.

370
00:35:49,131 --> 00:35:51,883
Don't you have anything to say to me?

371
00:35:56,346 --> 00:35:57,347
I'm sorry.

372
00:36:00,225 --> 00:36:01,977
I really am.

373
00:36:03,437 --> 00:36:04,688
I must've lost my mind.

374
00:36:07,024 --> 00:36:09,651
Thanks to you, I ended up
submitting a written apology

375
00:36:10,944 --> 00:36:12,654
and becoming an outcast.

376
00:36:13,739 --> 00:36:16,783
I know I deserve
what I'm going through.

377
00:36:18,535 --> 00:36:20,746
I'm having such a hard time
that I just want to quit.

378
00:36:22,956 --> 00:36:24,082
I know.

379
00:36:25,042 --> 00:36:26,501
Been there, done that.

380
00:36:29,296 --> 00:36:32,924
If we don't make up,
things won't get better for you.

381
00:36:35,886 --> 00:36:37,846
So what?

382
00:36:37,929 --> 00:36:39,431
Are you going to be the bigger person

383
00:36:40,390 --> 00:36:42,517
and forgive me or something?

384
00:36:43,769 --> 00:36:44,770
Not yet.

385
00:36:46,521 --> 00:36:47,522
But

386
00:36:48,940 --> 00:36:51,068
I will hold out a helping hand.

387
00:36:53,195 --> 00:36:55,238
If you actually feel bad

388
00:36:57,282 --> 00:36:58,575
will you help me?

389
00:37:01,703 --> 00:37:02,788
What?

390
00:37:03,830 --> 00:37:05,499
How can I help you?

391
00:37:06,458 --> 00:37:08,335
The HAN TFT proposal.

392
00:37:08,418 --> 00:37:11,171
It's way too hard for me.
You've written loads of proposals.

393
00:37:12,589 --> 00:37:13,965
Let's work on it together.

394
00:37:17,678 --> 00:37:18,762
Together?

395
00:37:19,221 --> 00:37:20,263
Yes.

396
00:37:24,267 --> 00:37:25,268
Sure. Whatever.

397
00:38:04,766 --> 00:38:07,102
Welcome.
Take your time to look around.

398
00:38:08,520 --> 00:38:10,439
- Can you take a look?
- Okay.

399
00:38:10,522 --> 00:38:13,024
Who's the director in charge
of this store?

400
00:38:13,567 --> 00:38:16,820
Oh, that would be
our Director Lee Chan.

401
00:38:20,240 --> 00:38:21,908
- I'll take this.
- Okay.

402
00:38:22,284 --> 00:38:23,910
You can pay over there.

403
00:38:45,557 --> 00:38:46,767
<i>Let's meet up.</i>

404
00:38:47,350 --> 00:38:48,393
<i>Stop avoiding me.</i>

405
00:38:59,237 --> 00:39:01,364
Are you Lee Chan?

406
00:39:06,536 --> 00:39:07,579
Han Jeong-yeon?

407
00:39:09,581 --> 00:39:10,916
- Let's talk another time.
- Okay.

408
00:39:15,003 --> 00:39:16,338
It really is you.

409
00:39:21,551 --> 00:39:23,011
When did you get to Korea?

410
00:39:25,055 --> 00:39:26,223
Just a few days ago.

411
00:39:27,390 --> 00:39:30,268
Has it been 15 years
since we last met?

412
00:39:32,437 --> 00:39:34,189
You never called once.

413
00:39:36,274 --> 00:39:37,609
Did you miss me?

414
00:39:43,031 --> 00:39:44,366
I remember the old days.

415
00:39:44,741 --> 00:39:46,618
They were the good times.

416
00:39:47,577 --> 00:39:49,996
You and I used to listen
to music at school.

417
00:39:51,790 --> 00:39:52,958
Do you remember?

418
00:39:53,041 --> 00:39:56,962
We promised to go to a jazz bar
for some live music and whiskey

419
00:39:57,045 --> 00:39:58,880
when you turned 20.

420
00:39:59,130 --> 00:40:01,091
You weren't there when I turned 20.

421
00:40:05,512 --> 00:40:06,638
I'm sorry about that.

422
00:40:09,516 --> 00:40:11,393
But I missed you guys, though.

423
00:40:14,145 --> 00:40:15,146
"You guys"?

424
00:40:16,523 --> 00:40:17,566
You and Ha-gi.

425
00:40:23,071 --> 00:40:24,155
Is he well?

426
00:40:25,615 --> 00:40:27,284
You two were inseparable.

427
00:40:28,618 --> 00:40:30,537
You haven't changed at all.

428
00:40:31,371 --> 00:40:33,999
- How so?
- How you make me uncomfortable.

429
00:40:38,670 --> 00:40:41,172
I thought becoming a celebrity
would've made you cool.

430
00:40:42,299 --> 00:40:43,383
You haven't changed either.

431
00:40:49,556 --> 00:40:52,267
I'm staying at the boutique hotel
across the road.

432
00:40:53,852 --> 00:40:54,978
See you again soon.

433
00:41:15,458 --> 00:41:18,879
You're incredibly good with a knife.

434
00:41:20,505 --> 00:41:22,132
I used to go by the nickname

435
00:41:22,382 --> 00:41:23,967
"Seocho's Knife-man."

436
00:41:26,011 --> 00:41:29,097
The stench of blood back then...

437
00:41:33,602 --> 00:41:35,437
"Knife-man"?

438
00:41:37,063 --> 00:41:38,481
That's in the past.

439
00:41:38,565 --> 00:41:40,775
Now I'm everyone's punching bag.

440
00:41:42,444 --> 00:41:45,363
<i>Was he disowned for having a record?</i>

441
00:41:46,031 --> 00:41:48,825
So what's your ideal type, Mi-mi?

442
00:41:50,869 --> 00:41:52,871
My ideal type?

443
00:41:53,455 --> 00:41:55,874
I like competent and capable men

444
00:41:57,334 --> 00:41:58,418
who are good kissers.

445
00:42:06,051 --> 00:42:08,219
That's a very clear answer.

446
00:42:08,845 --> 00:42:09,846
That's me.

447
00:42:18,438 --> 00:42:21,566
- I need to go to the ladies' room.
- Sure.

448
00:42:34,537 --> 00:42:35,664
My heart's racing.

449
00:42:38,959 --> 00:42:40,001
She wants to kiss already?

450
00:42:41,628 --> 00:42:43,046
That's way too fast.

451
00:42:44,255 --> 00:42:46,007
He looks incompetent.

452
00:42:48,343 --> 00:42:49,678
I bet he's a lousy kisser.

453
00:42:57,435 --> 00:42:59,145
Okay. Then what?

454
00:43:00,355 --> 00:43:01,564
You don't have a knife.

455
00:43:03,233 --> 00:43:05,110
How about we go
with kidnap and confinement?

456
00:43:05,902 --> 00:43:07,278
Murder is too much.

457
00:43:08,571 --> 00:43:11,282
Jeez. That's tricky.

458
00:43:13,868 --> 00:43:16,329
Something urgent came up.

459
00:43:16,746 --> 00:43:18,206
I have to dash.

460
00:43:18,289 --> 00:43:20,375
Mi-mi!

461
00:43:22,085 --> 00:43:23,461
Hold on, Mi-mi.

462
00:43:24,212 --> 00:43:25,755
Why is he following me?
Now I'm scared.

463
00:43:26,756 --> 00:43:28,633
What got into her? Mi-mi.

464
00:43:29,676 --> 00:43:31,594
Darn it.

465
00:43:38,685 --> 00:43:40,395
- I need help.
- With what?

466
00:43:40,729 --> 00:43:42,313
Someone's chasing me.

467
00:43:45,316 --> 00:43:46,609
My stomach hurts.

468
00:43:48,403 --> 00:43:50,363
You forgot your coat.

469
00:43:53,825 --> 00:43:55,285
ATTORNEY KIM MIN-WOO

470
00:43:56,494 --> 00:43:57,495
TRUE

471
00:44:00,915 --> 00:44:05,086
I don't know what you mistook me for,
but I really am an attorney.

472
00:44:05,170 --> 00:44:07,172
You know the state my body's in.

473
00:44:07,255 --> 00:44:12,260
What thug would have tech neck,
rounded shoulders, or a slipped disc?

474
00:44:12,343 --> 00:44:14,888
Why didn't you say so from the start?

475
00:44:14,971 --> 00:44:16,931
You never asked.

476
00:44:17,098 --> 00:44:18,433
It's not a good look

477
00:44:18,808 --> 00:44:21,644
to brag about your job
when no one asked.

478
00:44:32,405 --> 00:44:34,157
Does this look right?

479
00:44:34,449 --> 00:44:38,161
I wish we could add
a little something.

480
00:44:41,664 --> 00:44:42,707
Can you excuse me?

481
00:44:46,669 --> 00:44:47,921
Ms. Seo.

482
00:44:48,004 --> 00:44:50,381
This is my initial draft.

483
00:44:51,341 --> 00:44:52,342
How does it look?

484
00:44:57,472 --> 00:44:58,640
Oh, well...

485
00:44:59,224 --> 00:45:03,937
Page one makes the first impression,
and this looks too ordinary.

486
00:45:04,854 --> 00:45:07,148
It's always good
to put the conclusion first.

487
00:45:08,733 --> 00:45:09,943
In that case...

488
00:45:19,285 --> 00:45:20,286
This part...

489
00:45:20,537 --> 00:45:22,997
You two are working hard together.

490
00:45:29,379 --> 00:45:30,839
- Do this first.
- Okay.

491
00:45:31,089 --> 00:45:32,090
Then this.

492
00:45:32,173 --> 00:45:33,466
- Three, one, two?
- Yes.

493
00:45:33,550 --> 00:45:34,759
Okay. Got it.

494
00:45:55,905 --> 00:45:57,657
Let's go home, everyone.

495
00:45:58,575 --> 00:45:59,909
- Marketing Team.
- Yes?

496
00:45:59,993 --> 00:46:01,661
Look at the time.
Why are you still here?

497
00:46:01,744 --> 00:46:03,746
I still have work to do.

498
00:46:08,835 --> 00:46:10,879
You've got the gist of it.
You just need to fix the details.

499
00:46:11,129 --> 00:46:13,298
Finish it up tomorrow.
Rest is crucial for work.

500
00:46:13,548 --> 00:46:16,426
- Go on home.
- Can you review my proposal, too?

501
00:46:21,598 --> 00:46:23,808
- Go home.
- What? It's that perfect?

502
00:46:23,892 --> 00:46:26,060
You can't finish this today.
Do it over tomorrow.

503
00:46:27,395 --> 00:46:29,355
Okay, everyone. Pack up and go home.

504
00:46:29,439 --> 00:46:31,232
- Go home.
- But...

505
00:46:31,816 --> 00:46:33,109
- Bye.
- See you.

506
00:46:33,193 --> 00:46:34,903
- Let's all go home.
- Go home.

507
00:46:34,986 --> 00:46:36,779
- Okay.
- Go on home.

508
00:46:36,863 --> 00:46:38,531
- Good job, guys.
- Let's go.

509
00:46:40,116 --> 00:46:41,284
Finish it tomorrow.

510
00:47:11,773 --> 00:47:13,566
You can't really cook, can you?

511
00:47:13,900 --> 00:47:15,235
Well...

512
00:47:16,527 --> 00:47:18,404
I guess so.

513
00:47:18,696 --> 00:47:21,074
- I can't...
- I can't cook many things

514
00:47:21,157 --> 00:47:22,951
but I make a mean pasta.

515
00:47:24,702 --> 00:47:25,870
Do you?

516
00:47:26,246 --> 00:47:27,747
All you have to do is

517
00:47:28,706 --> 00:47:30,041
heat the bottled sauce
and add the pasta.

518
00:47:46,849 --> 00:47:47,850
Ms. Da-reum.

519
00:47:48,768 --> 00:47:49,894
Shall we swap tasks?

520
00:47:50,353 --> 00:47:51,396
Why?

521
00:47:51,562 --> 00:47:53,439
I'm really bad with knives.

522
00:47:53,898 --> 00:47:56,484
What? Step aside, then.
I'll take over.

523
00:48:43,990 --> 00:48:45,033
It's good.

524
00:48:45,450 --> 00:48:50,163
- You're great at cooking pasta.
- Right? I told you so.

525
00:48:50,663 --> 00:48:52,707
Eat at my place next time.

526
00:48:54,125 --> 00:48:55,918
At your place?

527
00:48:57,337 --> 00:48:59,756
The thing I'm second best at cooking

528
00:49:00,214 --> 00:49:01,507
is <i>tteokbokki.</i>

529
00:49:01,591 --> 00:49:02,675
We should have that next time.

530
00:49:06,012 --> 00:49:07,055
Okay, let's do that.

531
00:49:22,653 --> 00:49:23,654
So...

532
00:49:25,198 --> 00:49:26,949
You knew it was Ms. Seo.

533
00:49:28,326 --> 00:49:29,410
Why didn't you say so?

534
00:49:35,333 --> 00:49:38,461
I didn't want to suspect
for no good reason.

535
00:49:39,962 --> 00:49:41,839
You could've gone to anyone else

536
00:49:42,757 --> 00:49:44,175
for help with your proposal.

537
00:49:46,010 --> 00:49:47,678
I told you once before.

538
00:49:49,430 --> 00:49:50,515
I used to be an outcast.

539
00:49:55,186 --> 00:49:56,896
Looking at Ms. Seo made me think

540
00:49:58,064 --> 00:50:00,358
about how tormented she must feel.

541
00:50:01,859 --> 00:50:04,737
And also so lonely.

542
00:50:07,865 --> 00:50:09,617
That's what came to my mind first.

543
00:50:11,577 --> 00:50:12,912
I didn't want to see her...

544
00:50:16,541 --> 00:50:18,000
go through what I did.

545
00:50:19,836 --> 00:50:21,003
Ms. Da-reum.

546
00:50:23,172 --> 00:50:24,757
Despite being hurt yourself

547
00:50:25,758 --> 00:50:27,635
you choose to console others.

548
00:50:33,349 --> 00:50:36,227
That's what you did for me.

549
00:50:43,609 --> 00:50:44,735
Actually...

550
00:50:46,529 --> 00:50:48,030
I've lived my life
doing the opposite.

551
00:50:49,907 --> 00:50:52,493
I did my best
not to get too close to anyone.

552
00:50:54,537 --> 00:50:56,372
It's because
whenever I cherished someone...

553
00:51:01,752 --> 00:51:02,920
they ended up leaving me.

554
00:51:05,173 --> 00:51:06,174
It was easier...

555
00:51:08,092 --> 00:51:10,470
to throw myself into my work.

556
00:51:13,222 --> 00:51:14,348
You managed

557
00:51:15,600 --> 00:51:16,976
to break through that wall
to get to me.

558
00:51:41,167 --> 00:51:43,711
Do you remember this wine?

559
00:51:44,545 --> 00:51:47,882
Yes, it's the bottle I gifted you.

560
00:51:50,051 --> 00:51:51,135
The wine that helps

561
00:51:52,512 --> 00:51:53,596
one's love come true.

562
00:51:59,393 --> 00:52:00,436
It actually worked.

563
00:52:20,414 --> 00:52:21,666
MISSED CALL: HA-GI

564
00:52:21,749 --> 00:52:24,252
HA-GI: PLEASE PICK UP

565
00:52:55,241 --> 00:52:58,035
{\an8}APPELLO KANG HA-GI

566
00:53:00,746 --> 00:53:04,584
CEO KANG'S LEADERSHIP
SHINES THROUGH SCANDAL

567
00:53:04,667 --> 00:53:06,669
CEO KANG'S LEADERSHIP
SHINES THROUGH SCANDAL

568
00:53:51,411 --> 00:53:52,871
Why was it Ha-gi?

569
00:53:55,540 --> 00:53:56,541
What do you mean?

570
00:53:57,333 --> 00:53:58,751
You chose him.

571
00:54:01,588 --> 00:54:03,298
Why Ha-gi and not me?

572
00:54:12,724 --> 00:54:14,142
It was us first.

573
00:55:16,329 --> 00:55:17,538
<i>We met first.</i>

574
00:55:18,498 --> 00:55:19,582
<i>We connected first.</i>

575
00:55:20,291 --> 00:55:21,334
Hey, catch.

576
00:55:41,396 --> 00:55:42,855
<i>Whenever you smiled</i>

577
00:55:43,731 --> 00:55:45,525
<i>I thought I was the reason
you were smiling.</i>

578
00:56:01,207 --> 00:56:02,208
<i>So why</i>

579
00:56:04,210 --> 00:56:06,045
<i>did you choose Ha-gi in the end?</i>

580
00:56:17,473 --> 00:56:18,558
Tell me.

581
00:56:21,936 --> 00:56:22,979
The look in your eyes.

582
00:56:24,355 --> 00:56:25,648
It's the same as back then.

583
00:56:30,069 --> 00:56:32,155
You always wanted to rescue me.

584
00:56:34,323 --> 00:56:35,658
I felt grateful

585
00:56:37,243 --> 00:56:38,411
but I also hated it.

586
00:56:44,792 --> 00:56:45,793
Why?

587
00:56:47,170 --> 00:56:48,546
Your pity.

588
00:56:49,839 --> 00:56:51,340
You look at me
like I was unfortunate.

589
00:56:53,718 --> 00:56:54,969
Ha-gi didn't.

590
00:56:58,264 --> 00:56:59,432
He liked me...

591
00:57:01,434 --> 00:57:03,019
for who and what I was.

592
00:57:04,395 --> 00:57:06,064
I felt at ease around him.

593
00:57:11,027 --> 00:57:13,071
<i>I thought
if I were with someone I like</i>

594
00:57:13,529 --> 00:57:16,199
I'd be able to share
my feelings with him

595
00:57:16,699 --> 00:57:19,869
by laughing, crying

596
00:57:21,287 --> 00:57:23,414
whining, and even fighting.

597
00:57:24,540 --> 00:57:26,626
But for some reason

598
00:57:28,419 --> 00:57:29,420
I couldn't easily do that

599
00:57:31,047 --> 00:57:32,632
with you.

600
00:57:46,437 --> 00:57:49,607
Did something happen
between you and Ha-gi?

601
00:57:57,657 --> 00:57:58,741
No.

602
00:57:59,492 --> 00:58:01,869
I shouldn't have come. Take care.

603
00:58:02,578 --> 00:58:03,579
Chan.

604
00:58:09,377 --> 00:58:11,003
Do you need my help?

605
00:58:37,655 --> 00:58:40,741
See if you can win Ha-gi's heart.

606
00:59:13,024 --> 00:59:14,942
They never even called us back

607
00:59:15,193 --> 00:59:17,069
but they met up with SE Corporation.

608
00:59:18,571 --> 00:59:20,489
We lost out this time.

609
00:59:20,573 --> 00:59:21,824
Darn it.

610
00:59:30,917 --> 00:59:33,294
HAN DIDN'T CREATE A BRAND
BUT AN AESTHETIC

611
00:59:37,632 --> 00:59:39,091
Shall we return to the hotel?

612
00:59:39,800 --> 00:59:43,638
No, we have one more place to go.

613
00:59:44,931 --> 00:59:46,933
{\an8}CEO KANG HA-GI

614
00:59:51,646 --> 00:59:53,731
Mr. Kang.

615
00:59:54,565 --> 00:59:57,193
HAN's CEO is coming to visit Appello.

616
00:59:58,361 --> 01:00:00,363
- What?
- HAN, the brand.

617
01:00:00,446 --> 01:00:01,989
They're on their way.

618
01:00:20,508 --> 01:00:23,052
- Are they here?
- Yes.

619
01:01:18,065 --> 01:01:20,651
Meet HAN's CEO, Ms. Han Jeong-yeon.

620
01:01:24,488 --> 01:01:25,489
It's a pleasure.

621
01:01:25,990 --> 01:01:27,825
Welcome to Appello.

622
01:01:40,171 --> 01:01:42,840
Nice to meet you, Mr. Kang Ha-gi.

623
01:02:04,904 --> 01:02:08,491
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

624
01:02:19,627 --> 01:02:22,338
{\an8}EPILOGUE

625
01:02:50,032 --> 01:02:51,700
{\an8}Now, the five-second countdown.

626
01:02:51,784 --> 01:02:53,035
No, three seconds.

627
01:02:53,327 --> 01:02:57,123
- Three, two, one.
- Three, two, one.

628
01:02:59,250 --> 01:03:00,876
So about that.

629
01:03:00,960 --> 01:03:03,212
- The slides.
- Move the table here.

630
01:03:03,295 --> 01:03:04,797
- That should work.
- Okay.

631
01:03:04,880 --> 01:03:06,757
- That looks better.
- Right?

632
01:03:07,425 --> 01:03:08,884
- Yes.
- I think it's too big.

633
01:03:19,979 --> 01:03:22,773
They might as well broadcast
that they're dating.

634
01:03:22,857 --> 01:03:25,359
Right? They say when a couple
starts dating at work

635
01:03:25,443 --> 01:03:26,986
everyone knows about it,
even the water cooler.

636
01:03:42,251 --> 01:03:45,588
{\an8}WITNESS 1

637
01:03:45,671 --> 01:03:46,797
Let's start the meeting.

638
01:03:46,881 --> 01:03:48,048
- Okay.
- Okay.

639
01:03:50,926 --> 01:03:52,136
{\an8}ROMANTIC NIGHT VIEW SPOTS IN SEOUL

640
01:03:52,219 --> 01:03:53,387
{\an8}SEOUL NIGHT DATE IDEAS

641
01:03:55,055 --> 01:03:56,348
{\an8}WITNESS 2

642
01:04:00,394 --> 01:04:01,937
{\an8}WITNESS 3

643
01:04:07,151 --> 01:04:10,070
STORAGE

644
01:04:16,785 --> 01:04:20,331
Da-reum, Ms. Kim needs the sample
urgently. Have you found it?

645
01:04:20,414 --> 01:04:21,499
What?

646
01:04:21,582 --> 01:04:24,418
- Yes, I'm bringing it now.
- Okay.

647
01:04:32,635 --> 01:04:34,762
Let's pretend we have no idea.

648
01:04:34,845 --> 01:04:36,430
They're both clueless
when it comes to dating.

649
01:04:40,184 --> 01:04:41,352
- You're excited.
- Why are you so happy?

650
01:04:41,435 --> 01:04:43,479
It gives me butterflies.

651
01:04:44,021 --> 01:04:45,356
Haven't you ever been
in a relationship?

652
01:04:47,483 --> 01:04:49,818
{\an8}<i>Han Jeong-yeon?
She's Ha-gi's first love.</i>

653
01:04:49,902 --> 01:04:53,822
{\an8}If you ever make my Da-reum cry...

654
01:04:53,906 --> 01:04:55,574
{\an8}<i>The person who wrote that proposal...</i>

655
01:04:55,950 --> 01:04:58,077
{\an8}Would you like to lead the project?

656
01:04:58,619 --> 01:04:59,912
{\an8}<i>Why Ms. Da-reum of all people?</i>

657
01:05:00,412 --> 01:05:01,705
{\an8}<i>Whatever it may be</i>

658
01:05:02,331 --> 01:05:05,417
{\an8}I want you to do
what your heart tells you to do.

659
01:05:05,751 --> 01:05:08,420
{\an8}Does my relationship
with Mr. Kang bother you?

660
01:05:08,504 --> 01:05:12,466
{\an8}<i>- But I trust the person I'm dating.</i>
- Do you?

661
01:05:12,550 --> 01:05:13,592
{\an8}What does that mean?

662
01:05:13,717 --> 01:05:17,221
{\an8}<i>I want Ha-gi back.</i>

663
01:05:18,222 --> 01:05:20,891
{\an8}<i>Were you with her all this while?</i>

664
01:05:24,924 --> 01:05:26,926
{\an8}Subtitles by Eunjin Erica Kim
and Jennifer Jean Lim

665
